WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.114 --> 00:00:15.680
I was very tired, and I soon fell asleep.

2
00:00:17.221 --> 00:00:19.963
When I woke up, I didn't know where I was for a minute.

3
00:00:20.984 --> 00:00:24.066
I sat up and looked around, feeling a little scared.

4
00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:29.390
Then I remembered: I was hiding under some willows on the riverbank with the canoe.

5
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.373
I looked out across the Mississippi River; it was so wide.

6
00:00:35.093 --> 00:00:37.395
The other bank seemed far, far away.

7
00:00:39.556 --> 00:00:43.459
The moon was so bright I could have counted the logs that floated on the river.

8
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.601
Everything was quiet and it looked late.

9
00:00:47.622 --> 00:00:49.883
It even smelled late, if you know what I mean.

10
00:00:51.064 --> 00:00:56.107
I yawned and stretched and started to untie the canoe when I heard the sound of oars.

11
00:00:57.228 --> 00:00:59.910
Soon I saw a rowboat coming toward me.

12
00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:06.686
When it got closer, I saw that it was Pap, but he didn't see me because it was

13
00:01:06.746 --> 00:01:09.287
dark and I was hidden by the willow bushes.

14
00:01:10.568 --> 00:01:15.071
As soon as he was on shore, I started paddling as fast as I could to the middle

15
00:01:15.111 --> 00:01:15.591
of the river.

16
00:01:17.172 --> 00:01:21.474
Then I lay down in the bottom of the canoe and just let it float downstream.

17
00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:25.616
I listened to the sounds that carried over the water.

18
00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:29.679
I could even hear men talking on the ferry dock by the shore.

19
00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:34.281
As I floated farther, their voices faded slowly away.

20
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:40.045
Finally, I sat up and saw by the moonlight that I had come to Jackson's Island.

21
00:01:42.126 --> 00:01:46.268
I landed the canoe in a hollow on the shore of the island and covered it with willow

22
00:01:46.308 --> 00:01:48.270
branches so that no one could see it.

23
00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:54.473
As morning approached, the sky turned gray, and I went into the woods and had a nap.

24
00:01:56.835 --> 00:01:58.916
When I woke up, the sun was up high.

25
00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:04.014
I lay in the cool shade of the trees and felt rested and comfortable.

26
00:02:06.094 --> 00:02:10.976
A little breeze was blowing in the branches, and a couple of squirrels were chattering up there.

27
00:02:12.037 --> 00:02:12.957
I fell asleep again.

28
00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:16.939
I was awakened by a loud boom from the river.

29
00:02:18.079 --> 00:02:22.681
I peeked out from the trees and saw a ferryboat full of people out in the middle of

30
00:02:22.721 --> 00:02:23.101
the river.

31
00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:29.104
They were firing a cannon over the water, and I knew why they were doing it.

32
00:02:30.192 --> 00:02:34.414
They thought I was dead and they were trying to make my body rise up to the surface

33
00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:34.974
of the water.

34
00:02:36.095 --> 00:02:39.036
I went down to the riverbank and hid behind a log.

35
00:02:40.016 --> 00:02:44.518
As the ferryboat came closer to Jackson's Island, I looked through a hole in the log.

36
00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:51.441
I could see Pap, Judge Thatcher, Tom Sawyer, and lots of other people I knew from St.

37
00:02:51.481 --> 00:02:55.103
Petersburg. Everyone was talking about my murder.

38
00:02:56.183 --> 00:03:01.226
Then the captain said, "Maybe his body washed ashore and got tangled in the brush at the water's

39
00:03:01.326 --> 00:03:03.087
edge. I hope so, anyway."

40
00:03:04.668 --> 00:03:08.590
They all crowded up to the front of the boat and leaned over the rails, watching.

41
00:03:09.831 --> 00:03:12.352
I could see them clearly, but they couldn't see me.

42
00:03:13.273 --> 00:03:15.434
The boat floated on and went out of sight.

43
00:03:16.775 --> 00:03:20.117
I heard the cannon boom now and then, further and further off.

44
00:03:22.178 --> 00:03:25.460
After a while, I heard the boat on the other side of the island.

45
00:03:27.548 --> 00:03:30.549
It had turned around, and the people were going back to St.

46
00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:34.530
Petersburg. Now I guessed that they had stopped looking for me.

47
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:39.411
I got my supplies out of the canoe and made a nice camp in the woods.

48
00:03:40.632 --> 00:03:43.993
I made a tent out of my blankets to keep my things out of the rain.

49
00:03:45.173 --> 00:03:49.614
I caught a catfish, and around sunset, I lit a campfire and had supper.

50
00:03:51.695 --> 00:03:55.056
Then I set out a fishing line to catch some fish for breakfast.

51
00:03:56.212 --> 00:04:01.614
When the night became dark, I sat by my campfire, and as it got later, I felt lonely.

52
00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:07.756
I went down to the riverbank and listened to the river and counted the logs and rafts and

53
00:04:07.816 --> 00:04:10.576
stars. Finally, I went to bed.

54
00:04:12.677 --> 00:04:17.459
The next three days were exactly the same, but on the fourth day, I explored the island.

55
00:04:18.819 --> 00:04:21.620
It belonged to me and I wanted to know all about it.

56
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:26.152
I took my gun just in case I saw animals I could kill for food.

57
00:04:27.072 --> 00:04:33.098
I found lots of ripe strawberries, green summer grapes, and unripe raspberries I could eat later on.

58
00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.342
Then I almost stepped on a large snake.

59
00:04:39.003 --> 00:04:42.887
It slid off through the grass and flowers, and I ran after it, trying to shoot it.

60
00:04:44.088 --> 00:04:48.032
Suddenly I leaped onto the ashes of a campfire that was still smoking.

61
00:04:49.576 --> 00:04:52.798
My heart was beating so hard it was jumping out of my chest.

62
00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.962
I backed away as fast as I could, and then I ran.

63
00:04:59.303 --> 00:05:01.965
Every time I saw a bush, I thought it was a man.

64
00:05:03.006 --> 00:05:06.809
When I got back to camp, I hid all my supplies back in my canoe.

65
00:05:07.949 --> 00:05:10.271
I put out my campfire and climbed a tree.

66
00:05:11.892 --> 00:05:16.916
I couldn't stay up there forever, so finally I came down, but I stayed in the thick woods.

67
00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.381
By nighttime I was very hungry, but I was afraid to stay on the island.

68
00:05:23.642 --> 00:05:26.262
So I paddled my canoe over to the Illinois shore.

69
00:05:27.623 --> 00:05:31.964
I went into the woods there and had a meal of berries and the fish left over from

70
00:05:32.004 --> 00:05:32.604
my breakfast.

71
00:05:34.244 --> 00:05:39.906
I had just decided I would stay there all night when I heard horses coming, and then I

72
00:05:39.946 --> 00:05:40.926
heard men's voices.

73
00:05:42.187 --> 00:05:46.908
I was afraid they would see me, so I jumped into my canoe and paddled back to Jackson's

74
00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:47.208
Island.
